d  investigate  is the illegal israeli settlement on the  ground they hope that the icc's  prosecutor  would look into this as the main  violation of international law  and they believe that this has been a  policy by  the israeli authority it's not just a  war crime here or there  uh they believe that the foreign  ministry has released the statement as  you mentioned and they say that this  has been continuing and these work  crimes are ongoing which is why they  want the icc to investigate and  conclude its investigation urgently  nida the chief prosecutor of the icc  fatou bensouda  named the israeli army of course but  armed palestinian groups also such as  hamas as possible perpetrators of these  war crimes  what will be the reaction there from  these armed palestinian groups  especially at a time when different  palestinian factions have  tried to unite and bring about more  unity within palestine  when the icc's prosecutor said that she  believes that there are grounds for  opening an investigation that was  late in 2019 we seek the reaction from  the palestinian  factions including hamas and they have  said that they are  welcoming that they are they want to  have  an investigation by the international  criminal court  the palestinian factions are arguing and  they have been arguing for years now  that their  part that their armed resistance is part  of their  legal uh opposition and legal resistance  against the illegal israeli occupation  and this is why they hope that the icc  would focus  on the israeli crimes when it comes to  the gaza wars  but also and most importantly the  ongoing  continuous illegal settlement  construction in the occupied west bank  nida ibrahim in ramallah in the occupied  west bank thank you very much let's now  get the view  the uh view uh from israel harry foster  is in west jerusalem forest this is a  move harry that's always been  opposed by israel any early reactions  uh nothing that we've seen so far to  this precise step  but uh as nila was just just talking  about there was this decision  just last month by the panel of judges  to say that the uh the criteria had been  met for this to be  an investigation that could go forward  and at that point we heard  a very strong denunciation from the  prime minister benjamin netanyahu  of the endeavour saying that it was pure  anti-semitism  accusing the icc of being a politicized  institution  of course he worked very closely in  concert with the trump administration  to try to uh head this off uh the trump  administration issuing sanctions  against specific members of the  international criminal court that's  something that the bite administration  has been looking to unpick but the new  president biden  has also said through his officials  that he views this uh as something that  shouldn't go ahead  this investigation uh there's also been  comment from  prime minister benjamin netanyahu's uh  coalition partner  and shortly election rival benny gans  the defense minister  he was asked about this on tuesday  and he was saying that he was judging  himself as one of hundreds of people  who could be investigated and  potentially prosecuted  under this investigation of course the  icc uh investigates individuals  not states and he said that members of  the israeli military  uh would be protected and that he was at  that stage  hoping to try to head off this  investigation going forward now of  course we know  that it is going forward and as far as  israel is concerned  uh they challenge the legitimacy of the  process  thank you harry for that harry fossett  live for us today in west jerusalem  let's discuss all this further now with  ambassador  omar awa dalla who's head of the united  nations and human rights department at  the  palestinian ministry of foreign affairs  he's via skype from ramallah thank you  very much ambassador  for being with us says harry foster our  correspondent said there  the icc investigates individuals in this  case and not a state and already the  israeli prime minister  had said has said that he would protect  individuals within israel who are  suspected of these war crimes so  what is your reaction first to this icc  decision do you think it can achieve  justice definitely we believe that  the prosecutor uh did what she has with  its  obligation and under its mandate that's  why we saw it as a  victory for international law and  justice and that's why we welcome  the decision by the prosecutor to  investigate  the war crimes that committed committed  in the occupied palestinian territory  including east jerusalem we understand  that netanyahu and his  war criminal criminals they should be  afraid now from this  important body from this important stand  by the international criminal court this  as you say is about investigating war  crimes it's not necessarily about  determining  other issues in this conflict issues  like statehood and so on  so how does it help palestinians  it was very clear that there is nothing  to do with the issue of statehood and  that question was resolved actually  by the decision by the trial chamber  that  the issue of statehood is not the thing  that they are  looking in they are looking about the  jurisdiction of the international  criminal court and now  by the decision of opening the  investigation it's very clear that there  is  a important and territorial jurisdiction  of the international criminal court  where they can investigate war crimes  and crimes against  humanity that means that the era of  immunity for the israeli  officials is coming to an end and  within within the mandate of the  international criminal court  right it's not just israel however as  we've said palestinian factions  including hamas  are also likely to be investigated here  and the next step  in this will be to determine whether  israel or palestinian authorities have  investigations themselves and to assess  those so  how much cooperation can we expect from  the palestinian factions  we are ready uh we already we all uh  welcome the decision by the prosecutor  and before that we welcome the decision  by the british  chamber all the factions and the  government of the state of palestine we  all welcome this  decision and we are ready to cooperate  to coordinate with the  office of the prosecutor or the  investigator the investigators and  or any other advisors by the  international criminal court we will be  ready to cooperate and work closely with  the international criminal court  but we don't believe that israel is  going to investigate because  it is a policy it's a widespread and  systematic  policy of aggression against the  palestinian people  and crimes against the palestinian  people we don't believe  that there is any kind of investigation  in the israeli colonial regime and the  settlement regime  it's a governmental policy and a state  policy  indeed israel has already indicated at  least the prime minister has indicated  that it  didn't want to cooperate with this  investigation let me ask you a final  question ambassador  and this is about palestinian unity this  is coming at a time when  the various palestinian factions have  been trying to unite ahead of  uh elections that are coming up soon are  you concerned  that any investigation and its result a  conclusion  if it found let's say palestinian  factions also  guilty of war crimes would hamper these  efforts to bring about  unity we don't think that  as we said that all the factions the  factions and the government  they will come this decision and we are  going to coordinate we believe that our  unity is is a major and a better  issue in our march to freedom that's why  none the investigation or any other  issue can stop  this this process toward reconciliation  and having a unity between uh west bank  including jerusalem and gaza ambassador  thank you very much for talking to us  about this thank you for bring  giving us your reaction ambassador omar  award is head of  the united nations and human rights  department at the palestinian foreign  ministry

